From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Eby <kreed@kreed.org>
Date: Thu, 20 Aug 2026 00:22:41 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Run terminal children on the host

Terminal children run outside the sandbox on a real host PTY.
kitty-host-agent starts one ptyxis-agent on the host, has it create the
PTY and spawn the child there, and passes the PTY consumer descriptor
back over SCM_RIGHTS, so termios, resizes and job control work with no
relaying. A lifetime stub in its own process group stands in for the host
process, and the agent answers the cwd and foreground queries the sandbox
PID namespace hides.

Outside a Flatpak sandbox nothing here engages: should_run_on_host()
returns false, and fork() takes the unchanged sandbox path.
